\
* The analyses rely on six databases:\
		\'93electricity1.dta"  	- electricity data aggregating monthly information at the level of the research area\
		\'93electricity2.dta\'94		- electricity data aggregating information at the client level \
		\'93electricity3.dta\'94		- normalised electricity consumption data Goma to look at impact M23\
		\'93survey.dta\'94		- survey data\
		\'93acled.dta\'94			- monthly conflict events recorded by ACLED for the territories of our 3 research areas\
		\'93census.dta\'94		- census data\
\
* To replicate the tables and figures:\
		* Create a replication folder with subfolders \'93data\'94, \'93tables\'94, and \'93figures\'94\
		* Store the databases in the subfolder \'93data\'94\
		* Add the directory of the replication folder in the do-file \'93Replication.do\'94 and run the Stata do-file\
		* Tables and figures will be stored in the corresponding subfolders.\
\
\
* Please note that Figures 1 & 2 are maps that were created manually by the authors using QGIS - these are not reproduced by the do-file.\
* Please also note that some tables were created manually. These tables are not automatically stored as separate files in a subfolder; however, the do-file reproduces their contents in the Stata results window.\
}